---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
---

<Layout title="About" description="Queerview's mission and values.">
  <h1>About Queerview</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Queerview is a searchable, taggable database of film and television content featuring queer
    characters and/or created by queer people. It exists to help community members discover media,
    understand how their identities are represented, and contribute their knowledge to a shared
    resource.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>Values</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Truthfulness</strong> — tags are sourced and contestable, not authoritative by fiat.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Welcome</strong> — the experience should feel warm and accessible to anyone in or
        adjacent to the LGBTQ+ community, regardless of how they identify.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Humility</strong> — no single person's queer experience is universal; the system is
        designed to hold complexity rather than flatten it.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How tagging works</h2>
    <p>
      Contestation is displayed, not hidden — a character entry can be marked contested with notes
      explaining the disagreement. Facts and interpretation are kept separate: whether a character
      appears in a work is a fact, whether their portrayal constitutes a particular trope is an
      interpretation, and interpretive tags require a brief argument in their notes. Sources are
      weighted — claims sourced from public self-identification or explicit text carry more weight
      than inferred readings, and the site always surfaces which kind of source backs a tag.
    </p>
    <p>
      What is never up for debate: the validity of any identity in the vocabulary. See the
      <a href={withBase('tags')}>full tag vocabulary</a> for details.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>TMDB attribution</h2>
    <p>
      This product uses the TMDB API but is not endorsed or certified by TMDB. Title, cast, crew,
      and poster data comes from TMDB; all queer-specific metadata is maintained independently by
      Queerview.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .lede {
    max-width: 42rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  section {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  section h2 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
</style>
